{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-134156" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={6,\\,4,\\,6,\\,8},\\,y={3,\\,4,\\,5,\\,8}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=5.$ Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037644/state.json" "file_sha256" "582c25185fb0fb0685aa6f255b57631c8145344e585f1cc0eb7a4d9b7dc3bca8"} {"question" "q-134156" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(6-6)(3-5)+(4-6)(4-5)+(6-6)(5-5)+(8-6)(8-5)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(0)(-2)+(-2)(-1)+(0)(0)+(2)(3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+2+0+6] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037644/state.json" "file_sha256" "582c25185fb0fb0685aa6f255b57631c8145344e585f1cc0eb7a4d9b7dc3bca8"} {"question" "q-134156" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4e41ccb6ad2d8ba87fa45f035778c04ebb4af9eed446c2d379f9769591bc0ea"} {"question" "q-134156" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037644/state.json" "file_sha256" "582c25185fb0fb0685aa6f255b57631c8145344e585f1cc0eb7a4d9b7dc3bca8"} {"question" "q-134156" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037644/state.json" "file_sha256" "582c25185fb0fb0685aa6f255b57631c8145344e585f1cc0eb7a4d9b7dc3bca8"} {"question" "q-134156" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037644/state.json" "file_sha256" "582c25185fb0fb0685aa6f255b57631c8145344e585f1cc0eb7a4d9b7dc3bca8"} {"question" "q-134165" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={1,\\,4,\\,7,\\,12},\\,y={2,\\,4,\\,2,\\,8}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=4.$ Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037644/state.json" "file_sha256" "582c25185fb0fb0685aa6f255b57631c8145344e585f1cc0eb7a4d9b7dc3bca8"} {"question" "q-134165" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(1-6)(2-4)+(4-6)(4-4)+(7-6)(2-4)+(12-6)(8-4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-5)(-2)+(-2)(0)+(1)(-2)+(6)(4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[10+0-2+24] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 32 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037644/state.json" "file_sha256" "582c25185fb0fb0685aa6f255b57631c8145344e585f1cc0eb7a4d9b7dc3bca8"} {"question" "q-134165" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4e41ccb6ad2d8ba87fa45f035778c04ebb4af9eed446c2d379f9769591bc0ea"} {"question" "q-134165" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037644/state.json" "file_sha256" "582c25185fb0fb0685aa6f255b57631c8145344e585f1cc0eb7a4d9b7dc3bca8"} {"question" "q-134165" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2.5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "8.5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037644/state.json" "file_sha256" "582c25185fb0fb0685aa6f255b57631c8145344e585f1cc0eb7a4d9b7dc3bca8"} {"question" "q-134165" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037644/state.json" "file_sha256" "582c25185fb0fb0685aa6f255b57631c8145344e585f1cc0eb7a4d9b7dc3bca8"} {"question" "q-134168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y)$ for the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={-4,\\,2,\\,6,\\,8},\\,y={2,\\,-9,\\,3,\\,12}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037644/state.json" "file_sha256" "582c25185fb0fb0685aa6f255b57631c8145344e585f1cc0eb7a4d9b7dc3bca8"} {"question" "q-134168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot ((-4)+2+6+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =3 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (2+(-9)+3+12) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-4-3)(2-2)+(2-3)(-9-2)+(6-3)(3-2)+(8-3)(12-2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-7)(0)+(-1)(-11)+(3)(1)+(5)(10)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+11+3+50] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 64 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037644/state.json" "file_sha256" "582c25185fb0fb0685aa6f255b57631c8145344e585f1cc0eb7a4d9b7dc3bca8"} {"question" "q-134168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4e41ccb6ad2d8ba87fa45f035778c04ebb4af9eed446c2d379f9769591bc0ea"} {"questi